1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,830
Ew!

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,460
Ahhh! Ahaaahhhhh!

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,300
Ahaaahhhh!

4
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:11,240
Think of that steel block as Kaido Gamel!

5
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:16,540
Ahaaaaaahhhh!

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:18,830
Ahaaaah!

7
00:00:18,913 --> 00:00:19,743
Remember your defeat!

8
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:21,000
Your helplessness!

9
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,380
Hahh...

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,900
Ahhh...

11
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,777
Sunder...

12
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:28,860
Babla!

13
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,377
He's telling that to feel
like it's made of jelly.

14
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,290
No!

15
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,837
Five days remain until the raid.

16
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,817
We will move through Earth's horizon.

17
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:03,040
We will find infinity for sure.

18
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:07,660
Let's fight for this blue CLS to win.

19
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,020
Take us far away.

20
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:19,657
Don't give up so I can
come back to this moment.

21
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,900
So I can be present right here.

22
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:26,340
Throw away this rough sensation.

23
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:30,997
Shut it up, do not be
so afraid to podcast.

24
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,697
You have a friend right here.

25
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:37,057
And I will always be here by your side.

26
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,697
To take care of you.

27
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:43,977
Even in the darkest of times I'll try.

28
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:46,517
Look and brave it out, it's alright.

29
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,737
Cause we are the ones who
are meant to rule the law.

30
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:53,457
We will move towards the horizon.

31
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:56,397
We will find insanity for sure.

32
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:59,217
We're a world step ahead.

33
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,177
We will win for sure.

34
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,257
Dreaming on.

35
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:04,677
We will move towards the horizon.

36
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,597
We will fight however we can.

37
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:10,517
In order to be the best we will run.

38
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,217
To the top, to the end.

39
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:19,040
We gotta be the ones that
just keep dreaming on.

40
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:22,157
I just can't give up now.

41
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,917
I can never stop cause.

42
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,377
I gotta give everything I got to.

43
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:32,180
Become the greatest of all times.

44
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:35,857
We will move towards the horizon.

45
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:38,977
We will find things we need for sure.

46
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:41,257
We will step back.

47
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,517
And we will wait for sure.

48
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,720
So keep moving on.

49
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,830
Oh!

50
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,160
Greetings, my friends.

51
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,460
This is Kinamon.

52
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,779
Pull out your flyers, if you would.

53
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,100
I need you to make an alteration.

54
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:17,560
Add two lines to the Habu Viper's belly.

55
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:22,600
Doing so, we'll reveal Lord
Yasui's message to you.

56
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:29,320
Like this.

57
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,980
Two lines.

58
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:40,020
Oh, yes, that makes sense.

59
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:43,360
Yasui's quite clever.

60
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,520
I see.

61
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,040
We got it.

62
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,280
Looking good.

63
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:53,637
Hey, put your hips into it.

64
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:56,617
We'll be sailing through rough
waters to reach Onigashima.

65
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:57,917
We need something sturdy.

66
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,220
You got it, boss!

67
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,265
Mine's on the viper's stomach.

68
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,860
Oh, of course.

69
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,280
I understand, Sakine-mona.

70
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:06,870
Excellent.

71
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,180
Then all is well.

72
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:09,630
Hmm?

73
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,380
Sakine-mona here?

74
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:14,220
I'm getting those ships in tip-top shape.

75
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:15,650
Super!

76
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,980
Look forward to it.

77
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,480
We got this!

78
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:20,720
Don't you worry!

79
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,180
Count on us!

80
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:23,637
I'll go spread the word.

81
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,677
Everyone will know about the change.

82
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:26,900
You have my thanks.

83
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:29,039
Pretty impressive.

84
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:31,737
The people from Wano
can take one look at the

85
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:33,937
flyer and understand the
message in an instant,

86
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:34,850
huh?

87
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:35,763
Hmm.

88
00:04:35,846 --> 00:04:37,721
Let's see if I can figure it out.

89
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,020
You add two lines to Viper.

90
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:43,650
Viper?

91
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,700
Uh, well, no.

92
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:50,240
One cannot understand it unless
they know the names of Wano's ports.

93
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,600
Itachi Port.

94
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,360
At any rate, the point is,

95
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:08,971
each of these ports is associated
with a particular animal.

96
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,217
So with the initial image of the viper,

97
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:14,594
we implied that Habu port
would be the rendezvous point.

98
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:17,260
But if you add two lines to a viper,

99
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,377
then they appear as legs, and
with a moment's consideration,

100
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:23,225
the image of a lizard
will likely come to mind.

101
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,911
Tokage Port is associated with the Lizard.

102
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:30,677
So, our allies will understand that our
new rendezvous point is the port in Udon.

103
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,557
The flyer is considered a prank,

104
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:35,237
so there is little chance
that our foes will catch on.

105
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,800
It's truly a marvel.

106
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,697
Lord Yasui deceived the enemy and gave our

107
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,545
thwarted plan a path
forward in one fell swoop.

108
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,740
Our ally to the bitter end.

109
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,675
Alas, it is a debt we can never repay.

110
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:55,700
If we put his efforts to waste,
it will be our shame as Samurai.

111
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:59,040
I'm suddenly reminded of his words.

112
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,360
Do you remember what he told us?

113
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:05,440
We'll become the guardian
deities of Wano itself.

114
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,597
A brilliant man.

115
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,000
Taken too soon.

116
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:18,460
Of course, a few challenges yet remain,
but we owe much to your efforts.

117
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,830
Furthermore,

118
00:06:22,913 --> 00:06:26,097
our number of allies has increased
and our friends have been reassembled.

119
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:29,017
Although Dintudo's whereabouts
are still a mystery.

120
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,220
We have seven of the Yakuzaia 9!

121
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,060
All as strong as ever!

122
00:06:44,860 --> 00:06:46,500
This turned around fast.

123
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,017
I think we got a shot.

124
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:51,180
We need 5,000 troops, right? Correct.

125
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,501
And we're close.

126
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,512
Let's stop patting ourselves on the back.

127
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:58,580
We're wasting valuable time.

128
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:00,530
All right.

129
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:03,940
In that case, let's discuss the plan.

130
00:07:04,580 --> 00:07:08,420
We'll take Kaido's head at any
cost, and Orochi's as well.

131
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:11,120
We shall do more than avenge Lord Odin.

132
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:13,040
We'll save this land.

133
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:17,540
Check it out!

134
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,480
A piece of trivia.

135
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,020
For those determined enough,

136
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:29,277
there were actually two ways
to enter the land of water.

137
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:32,713
The first is the dangerous
path that the Straw Hats took,

138
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:35,600
carried up the waterfalls
by giant koi fish.

139
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:42,220
The other is to pass through a massive
cave hidden behind one of the waterfalls.

140
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,700
Needless to say,

141
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:49,216
this will not end well for those
without Kaido and Orochi's permission.

142
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:52,740
At the end of the cave lies Mogara port.

143
00:07:56,620 --> 00:08:00,780
From there, a gondola will haul up
both crew and cargo to the surface.

144
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,800
After a short trip,
they'll exit the tunnel.

145
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:13,760
And at last, find themselves in Hakamai.

146
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:18,660
Ring-a-ding-ding, Kaido, sir.

147
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,296
We're in the house, as one might say.

148
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:23,980
Ah, just in time.

149
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:28,147
Didn't think you'd bother coming
back here for the party, Apu.

150
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,537
Wouldn't miss it for the world.

151
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:34,738
The Golden Festival is here,
and it's gonna be tight!

152
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,680
I never skip out on a party,
or give up on a fight!

153
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,560
It's gonna be wild this year, trust me.

154
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,760
My kind of scene! Yeah!

155
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:47,340
Now groove with me, boys!

156
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,380
What are those things?

157
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,620
It's the numbers.

158
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:11,280
The numbers from Wakakashima.

159
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:13,140
Let's run now.

160
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,180
Or they'll eat us.

161
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,915
Sounds like the numbers have returned.

162
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:25,677
Those are some messy drunks
if I've ever seen them.

163
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:26,995
Tell them to go away.

164
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,557
This is just a warm-up.

165
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:32,120
The real party's right around the corner.

166
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:35,000
I'll drink to that one more round.

167
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,540
The hell.

168
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:41,548
They were trying to
kill each other earlier.

169
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,760
Hey, listen up, boys.

170
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,250
Uh, yeah?

171
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:52,380
We got some important news
about the Beast Pirates.

172
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,840
And the Big Mom Pirates, too.

173
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,057
Let me stand up.

174
00:09:57,140 --> 00:10:00,200
We have decided to form an alliance.

175
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:01,810
Hooray!

176
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:04,970
What?

177
00:10:05,053 --> 00:10:09,180
So first things first, we combine
our strength and conquer the world!

178
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:12,860
Then we can go back to killing each other.

179
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:27,970
Is this true?

180
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:30,400
You do not jest! Tell me!

181
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,780
Yes, it's true.

182
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,520
What a blessed day!

183
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:37,560
Lady Hiyori is alive and
well! That's correct.

184
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,720
I was relieved as well.

185
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,320
My heart aches for Otoko.

186
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,500
She has endured so much pain.

187
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:50,252
She needs some time to adjust
and will require a guardian.

188
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:53,960
For now, I shall refrain
from meeting with everyone.

189
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,240
It's for the best.

190
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,757
sentimentality has no place in battle.

191
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:03,457
Please lend them your strength.

192
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:05,037
Go to the others.

193
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:08,457
Find a way to protect the land of Wano.

194
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:12,237
Princess this is unnecessary.

195
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:14,040
Please stand up.

196
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,837
You're certain it's her, our
little tomboy's become so elegant.

197
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:27,057
My she's truly grown up.

198
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:31,677
Oh Koamatsu, learning of your
imprisonment, we truly fared for the worst.

199
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:32,760
That's wonderful.

200
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,477
She lives.

201
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,757
I try to do a ha ha ha.

202
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,017
School where is she now?

203
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,097
Is she guarded?

204
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:42,077
No need to fear.

205
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,620
She is in a safe place at the moment.

206
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:48,020
This is so delightful to hear.

207
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,980
What a tremendous relief!

208
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:55,700
She's still alive.

209
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,160
Mama Nisuke!

210
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,840
Hiyori! Drop!

211
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,160
No!

212
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,510
Hiyori...

213
00:12:15,593 --> 00:12:16,740
Zorojuro!

214
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:20,158
So you were the one who rescued her?

215
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,720
I am grateful.

216
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:25,980
She hacks a bit rough and tumble,
but she's actually fragile.

217
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,913
That crybaby could be quite the handful.

218
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,070
Easy there.

219
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:32,789
That crybaby's 18 years
older than you now.

220
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:36,219
You really gotta get your
mind out of the past, bud.

221
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,330
Whoa!

222
00:12:37,413 --> 00:12:38,243
Ah!

223
00:12:38,326 --> 00:12:39,156
Ah!

224
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:42,530
Ah!

225
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,220
K! Oh no!

226
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,820
So she has a Heinen age advantage now?

227
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:49,860
I never considered that. Ah!

228
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:53,772
How long have you known, and
you didn't bother telling me?

229
00:12:53,860 --> 00:12:56,140
That goddess is Momonosuke's sister?

230
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,630
Ah!

231
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,190
What?

232
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:02,640
Stop staring.

233
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,010
Ah!

234
00:13:06,093 --> 00:13:07,620
Hey, little buddy.

235
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:11,060
If you need anything, just
come to Uncle Sangoro.

236
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,301
I know exactly what you're doing.

237
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:17,120
Sir Sangoro, that's enough fooling around.

238
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,496
Kawamatsu, preparations are complete.

239
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:23,840
It's still not too late.

240
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,500
Are you quite sure?

241
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:29,080
Yes, we have already come to an agreement.

242
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:32,380
Sir Hitetsu, this is for you.

243
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:33,837
It's Kitetsu II.

244
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:34,750
Second.

245
00:13:34,833 --> 00:13:37,960
It was confiscated from
Luffy Taro and Udon. Here.

246
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,420
Thank you kindly.

247
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:42,115
He took it from me without permission.

248
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,710
Kitetsu.

249
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,640
I had a feeling it was a famed blade.

250
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:54,460
Now, my name is Tenguyama Hitetsu.

251
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,380
I am a swordsmith from the land of Wano.

252
00:13:58,740 --> 00:13:59,677
Today's the day.

253
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,140
For two decades,

254
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:05,517
I have awaited the opportunity to be
in your presence, Lord Momonosuke.

255
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,080
I now bequeath these swords to you.

256
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,940
These were once Lord
Oden's precious weapons.

257
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,660
Ame no Habakiri,

258
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:23,257
the one who cuts down the highest heavens,

259
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:27,160
and Enma, the one who slices
through the deepest hells.

260
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:34,120
Like Shusui, they stand among legends
as two of the 21 excellent Greyblades

261
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:38,494
What would you like to do
with my masterpieces, my lord?

262
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:40,000
The choice is yours.

263
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:42,337
I'm not ready.

264
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:45,377
But do not mistake this feeling for fear.

265
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:48,695
I'd merely prefer it if you
kept it for the time being.

266
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:53,060
As for Enma, it now belongs to you.

267
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,677
However, please heed my warning!

268
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:01,320
The only man who has ever tamed
that blade was Kozuki Odin himself.

